    "detailed_description": "Flea was designed for the NES and dose run on an actual NES But is now on Steam!<br><br>Flea is a challenging 2D platformer with an intriguing back story. Play as Henry the Hyperactive Flea who just can\u2019t stop jumping! Navigate the beasts and collect blood to get the heart of the problems. <br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Explore 80 levels<br></li><li>Meet weird characters<br></li><li>Discover secrets.</li></ul><br>This game was funded with Kickstarter this leap year!",
    "about_the_game": "Flea was designed for the NES and dose run on an actual NES But is now on Steam!<br><br>Flea is a challenging 2D platformer with an intriguing back story. Play as Henry the Hyperactive Flea who just can\u2019t stop jumping! Navigate the beasts and collect blood to get the heart of the problems. <br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Explore 80 levels<br></li><li>Meet weird characters<br></li><li>Discover secrets.</li></ul><br>This game was funded with Kickstarter this leap year!",
    "short_description": "Flea is a challenging retro 2D platformer with an intriguing back story.",
    "supported_languages": "English",
    "reviews": "\u201cThe pixels are colourful, the action is smooth, but this isn't the sort of title that's going to push the hardware. That doesn't matter at all, of course, as the core gameplay is fun and challenging enough to justify itself a place in the library.\u201d<br>NA \u2013 The Dreamcast Junkyard<br><br>\u201cFlea is a stunningly good independent game with a unique mechanic that is bound to make the retrogamer in us all smile and laugh our heads off whilst keeping the difficulty curve to make this game good for speed running. In my opinion, this game is good and addictive enough to be the next Super Meat Boy, and is also family friendly enough that both the dad and the kids in the family will want to play it. Also, it\u2019s been the most fun I\u2019ve had in reviewing a game for ages.\u201d<br>NA \u2013 GamerHub<br><br>\u201cIn short, Flea! is a great example that many systems that some believe are obsolete have a lot to give, since in this case it has been possible to adapt a genre that is very dynamic and demanding such as precision platforms in a very well achieved and polished way, resulting in a very pleasant experience that leaves a good taste in the mouth.\u201d<br>NA \u2013 Retro -o- Rama<br>",
